      "a0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001": {
        "tag": "rich-text",
        "id": "a0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
        "content": "# Mitsein: Human → World ← Human\n\nMitsein is NOT a morphism between vats. It is a **span**:\n\n```\nHuman → World ← Human\n```\n\nNeither human has direct access to the other. They meet IN the world. The world is the mediating object — the shared plane where projection happens. Both agents project into it. Neither owns it.\n\nThis is the fundamental correction to the entire framework:\n- NOT: Vat → Vat (direct morphism)\n- YES: Vat → World ← Vat (span through shared context)\n\n## Span Composition (Pullback)\n```\nA → W₁ ← B → W₂ ← C\n       composes via pullback at B:\nA → W₁ ×_B W₂ ← C\n```\n\nB doesn't just relay — B co-constitutes the composed world. The pullback IS the shared context.\n\n## Instances\n| Left | World | Right | Module |\n|------|-------|-------|--------|\n| Human | CapTPSession | Human | tcp_transport.zig |\n| Tablet | ReelPlane | Tablet | cell_dispatch.zig |\n| Agent | TaskList | Agent | team coordination |\n| Tree | EditPath (TreeDiff) | Tree | syrup.zig |\n| Actor | Actormap (transactional heap) | Actor | worlds/world.zig |\n| Vat | Bootstrap Object | Vat | message_frame.zig |\n\n## 326 Worlds (world_enum.zig)\nEach world is a meeting point, not a container:\n- WorldConfig: variant (A/B/C) × trit[7] × depth\n- GF(3) conservation: only balanced worlds survive filtering\n- Necklace reduction: mod rotational symmetry\n- De Bruijn window: every local pattern appears once\n- 326 = the number of maximally interesting meeting points\n\n## GF(3) of the Span\n- Left projection: +1 (Generator — the one who initiates)\n- World: 0 (Coordinator — the shared meeting place)\n- Right projection: -1 (Validator — the one who responds/validates)\n- Sum: (+1) + 0 + (-1) = 0 ✓\n\nBut the roles are symmetric! Either human can be +1 or -1. The world is always 0. This is Heidegger's point: Mitsein is equiprimordial. Neither party is ontologically prior."
      },
