      "a0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000040": {
        "tag": "rich-text",
        "id": "a0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000040",
        "content": "## The 326 Worlds as Span Vertices\n\nEach WorldConfig in world_enum.zig is a potential meeting point:\n- Variant A/B/C = the three URI schemes (a://, b://, c://)\n- Trit sequence = the path through GF(3) state space\n- Conservation filter = only balanced worlds survive\n- Necklace reduction = symmetry up to rotation (the span is symmetric!)\n\nThe 326 worlds are exactly the maximally interesting vertices in the bicategory of spans. They are the non-trivial, conserved, rotationally-reduced meeting points.\n\n## Diffusion on Spans\n\nTree diffusion on Mitsein is not diffusion on vats. It is diffusion on the **worlds between them**:\n- Forward noise: corrupt the shared world (mutate the meeting point)\n- Reverse denoise: reconstruct the shared world from both projections\n- The denoising is inherently multi-agent: both participants contribute to reconstruction\n- Grammar constraint: the shared world must remain a valid meeting point (conserved, balanced)\n\nThis is why the ncreel layout starts from the focused tablet. The focus IS one agent's projection. The layout algorithm reconstructs the shared world (ReelPlane) from that projection, then incorporates others."
      }
